<div class="legende-triplex">
    <span><span class="pastille laon"></span>Laon, above&nbsp;: where to press on, where to settle</span>
    <span><span class="pastille vat"></span>Square notation, centre&nbsp;: the notes of the jubilus</span>
    <span><span class="pastille sg"></span>St. Gall, below&nbsp;: the gesture, the episemas</span>
</div>

<div class="encadre">
    <span class="etiquette">Key point for this chant</span>
    <p>
        The Alleluia is the form in which <strong>the melisma becomes the
        subject</strong>&nbsp;: one word, an explosion of notes, a verse, and off we go
        again. Now listen to the same genre at the other great pole of the liturgical
        year&nbsp;: Easter.
    </p>
</div>

